# Project Statement

## Project Title
Library Book Management System

## Objective
To develop a simple console-based Library Book Management System in Python that allows users to efficiently manage books in a library. The system provides basic functionalities for adding books, borrowing, returning, and viewing the book collection.

## Problem Statement
Manual book management in small libraries or educational institutions can be time-consuming and prone to errors. There is a need for a lightweight, easy-to-use digital system that can track book availability, handle borrowing and returning processes, and maintain an updated record of all books without requiring complex setup or database knowledge.

## Scope
This project is a beginner-friendly Python application focused on core library operations. It uses in-memory storage and a command-line interface, making it ideal for learning Python programming concepts such as functions, dictionaries, loops, and user input handling.

## Key Features
- Add new books or increase the number of copies of existing books
- Borrow a book if copies are available
- Return a previously borrowed book
- Display a list of all books with title, author, available copies, and total copies
- Simple and intuitive menu-driven interface

## Technologies Used
- Python 3
- Built-in data structures (Dictionary)

## Limitations
- Data is not persistent (lost when the program is closed)
- No user authentication
- No advanced features like due dates, fines, or search functionality

## Target Users
- Students learning Python
- Small libraries or personal book collections
- Beginners who want to build a complete mini-project

## Future Enhancements
- Save and load data using JSON file
- Search books by title or author
- Add due dates and fine calculation
- Simple graphical user interface (GUI)
- Book deletion and editing
